[center][size=5][b][color=#f0c850]QuickGPS[/color][/b][/size]
[size=3]A quick GPS menu for GTA IV: mission givers and the nearest services, one click away.[/size][/center]

[line]

[size=4][b]What it does[/b][/size]
Hold [b]Tab[/b] for a second and a panel opens in the top-left corner listing:
[list]
[*][b]Mission givers:[/b] every contact on the map (Roman, Little Jacob, Brucie, strangers, assassination jobs and so on), nearest first.
[*][b]Nearest services:[/b] the closest one of each kind: Hospital, Gun Shop, Pay 'n' Spray, Clothes Shop, Burger Shot, Internet Cafe, Safehouse, Train Station, Taxi Rank, Bar, Bowling and more.
[/list]
Scroll to one and left click. A yellow destination marker appears on the map with a GPS route to it, and a small line in the top-left shows the place, the distance and which way to go ("ahead-left"). The route clears itself when you arrive.

[size=4][b]Features[/b][/size]
[list]
[*]Hold-to-open with a progress bar, so a quick tap of Tab does nothing.
[*]Niko keeps walking or driving while the menu is open. The game never sees your clicks or scroll wheel while it's open, so he won't shoot, aim or switch weapons.
[*]On-screen distance and direction hint, handy on foot since GTA IV only draws the route line while you're in a vehicle.
[*]Change the hotkey in game (SETTINGS > Change hotkey). Hold time, mouse buttons, scroll direction, miles and more are in [b]QuickGPS.ini[/b].
[/list]

[size=4][b]Controls[/b][/size]
[list]
[*][b]Hold Tab (1 s)[/b]: open the menu
[*][b]Mouse wheel[/b]: move the selection
[*][b]Left click[/b]: set a route to the selection
[*][b]Right click[/b] or [b]Tab[/b]: close the menu
[*][b]F9[/b]: write a list of every map blip to [i]scripts\QuickGPS_blips.txt[/i] (for bug reports)
[/list]

[size=4][b]Requirements[/b][/size]
[list]
[*]GTA IV: The Complete Edition [b]1.2.0.59[/b] (tested). 1.0.7.0 / 1.0.8.0 should work with a matching ScriptHookDotNet but haven't been tested.
[*]An ASI loader ([url=https://github.com/ThirteenAG/Ultimate-ASI-Loader/releases]Ultimate ASI Loader[/url]; FusionFix setups already have one).
[*][url=https://github.com/Tomasak/gta4_scripthookdotnet/releases]ScriptHookDotNet, Tomasak's Complete Edition fork[/url] (tested with v1.7.1.8).
[*].NET Framework 4.x (preinstalled on Windows 10 and 11).
[/list]

[size=4][b]Install[/b][/size]
[list=1]
[*]Back up your saves ([i]Documents\Rockstar Games\GTA IV\[/i]).
[*]Install ScriptHookDotNet into the folder that holds [b]GTAIV.exe[/b], following its readme.
[*]Extract the QuickGPS zip into that same folder. It adds [i]scripts\QuickGPS.net.dll[/i] and [i]scripts\QuickGPS.ini[/i].
[*]Load a save and hold Tab.
[/list]
If nothing shows up, check [i]ScriptHookDotNet.log[/i] in the GTAIV folder.
[b]Uninstall:[/b] delete [i]scripts\QuickGPS.net.dll[/i] and [i]scripts\QuickGPS.ini[/i].

[size=4][b]Notes[/b][/size]
[list]
[*]Only blips the game has placed are listed, so story contacts appear as they unlock.
[*]Contacts from The Lost and Damned and The Ballad of Gay Tony show up as "Contact #id".
[*]Don't also put a QuickGPS.cs in the scripts folder: it would load twice.
[*]Single-player only.
[/list]

[size=4][b]Source code[/b][/size]
QuickGPS is open source under the MIT License. Source, build scripts, issues and releases are on GitHub:
[url=https://github.com/Darjjj/QuickGPS]https://github.com/Darjjj/QuickGPS[/url]
Found a bug? Open an issue there or post in the comments, ideally with your [i]QuickGPS_blips.txt[/i] (press F9 in game).

